{"source":"nco2015","code":"7421.1101","level":5,"parent_code":"7421","parent_source":"isco08","isco_major":"7","isco_unit":"7421","skill_level":null,"label_en":"Repair Assistant: Switches","label_hi":null,"description_en":"Repair Assistant is responsible for diagnosing the faulty sub system and addressing first-level complaints and servicing of industrial-communications switches. The individual at work diagnoses and carries out repairs communication switches by dismantling, removing and replacing faulty systems or sub systems or assembly. Qualification Pack Details: QP NOS Reference ELE/Q8103 QP NOS Name Repair Assistant: Switches NSQF Level 4","selectable":true,"status":"active","industry_id":null,"canonical_role_id":null,"aliases":[{"text":"Repair Assistant: Switches","lang":"en","source":"nco2015"}]}
{"source":"nco2015","code":"7421.1001","level":5,"parent_code":"7421","parent_source":"isco08","isco_major":"7","isco_unit":"7421","skill_level":null,"label_en":"Field Engineer-RACW","label_hi":null,"description_en":"Field Engineer-RAWC is also, called `Service Engineer', the Field Engineer provides installation and after sales service on multiple appliances such as refrigerator, air conditioner and washing machine. The individual at work interacts with customers to install the appliance and diagnose the problem to assess possible causes of malfunction. Once the problem and causes have been identified, the individual rectifies minor problems or replaces faulty modules for failed parts or recommends factory repairs for bigger faults. Qualification Pack Details: QP NOS Reference ELE/Q3105 QP NOS Name Field Engineer- RAWC NSQF Level 4 LUME II B 226 Divison 7","selectable":true,"status":"active","industry_id":null,"canonical_role_id":null,"aliases":[{"text":"Field Engineer-RACW","lang":"en","source":"nco2015"}]}
{"source":"nco2015","code":"7421.1201","level":5,"parent_code":"7421","parent_source":"isco08","isco_major":"7","isco_unit":"7421","skill_level":null,"label_en":"Auto-Tester Capacitor","label_hi":null,"description_en":"Auto-Tester programs the auto testing machine for segregating defective capacitors from passed ones. The individual at work is responsible for testing the capacitor using automated testing machine for electrical, tan-delta and capacitance as per machine specifications. Qualification Pack Details: QP NOS Reference ELE/Q0103 QP NOS Name Auto-tester Capacitor NSQF Level 4 VOL National Classification of Occupations - 2015 QP NOS Name NSQF Level TV Repair Technician 4","selectable":true,"status":"active","industry_id":null,"canonical_role_id":null,"aliases":[{"text":"Auto-Tester Capacitor","lang":"en","source":"nco2015"}]}
{"source":"nco2015","code":"7421.1202","level":5,"parent_code":"7421","parent_source":"isco08","isco_major":"7","isco_unit":"7421","skill_level":null,"label_en":"Testing Technician","label_hi":null,"description_en":"Testing Technician sorts, inspects and tests the resistors and capacitors to check value and conformance with specified standards. The individual at work is responsible for testing the resistor or capacitor using test and measuring equipment, jigs and visual aids in order to ensure that they are of correct value, and are painted and marked as per company's specifications. Qualification Pack Details: QP NOS Reference ELE/Q0111 QP NOS Name Testing Technician- Passive components NSQF Level 4","selectable":true,"status":"active","industry_id":null,"canonical_role_id":null,"aliases":[{"text":"Testing Technician","lang":"en","source":"nco2015"}]}
{"source":"nco2015","code":"7421.1301","level":5,"parent_code":"7421","parent_source":"isco08","isco_major":"7","isco_unit":"7421","skill_level":null,"label_en":"TV Repair Technician","label_hi":null,"description_en":"TV Repair Technician is also, called `Field Technician-TV', the TV Repair Technician provides after sales service to customers. The individual at work interacts with customers to install the TV as well as diagnose the problem and assess possible causes of fault reported. Once the problem and causes have been identified, the individual rectifies minor problems or replaces faulty modules for failed parts or recommends factory repairs for bigger faults. Qualification Pack Details: QP NOS Reference ELE/Q3105 LUME II B 227 Divison 7 layout requirement as per design, assesses precautionary measures to be taken, installs the solar panel as per customer's requirement and ensures effective functioning of the system post installation. Qualification Pack Details: QP NOS Reference ELE/Q5901 QP NOS Name Solar Panel Installation Technician NSQF Level 4","selectable":true,"status":"active","industry_id":null,"canonical_role_id":null,"aliases":[{"text":"TV Repair Technician","lang":"en","source":"nco2015"}]}
{"source":"nco2015","code":"7421.1302","level":5,"parent_code":"7421","parent_source":"isco08","isco_major":"7","isco_unit":"7421","skill_level":null,"label_en":"Field Engineer TV","label_hi":null,"description_en":"Field Engineer TV is also called, `Service Engineer - TV', the TV Field Engineer provides installation and after sales service to buyers of TV and other consumer electronic products such as home theatre system, DVD and Blu-ray players, audio systems, headphones etc. The individual at work interacts with customers to install the entertainment system and diagnose any problems to assess possible causes of malfunction. Once the problem and causes have been identified, the individual rectifies minor problems or replaces faulty modules for failed parts or recommends factory repairs for bigger faults. Qualification Pack Details: QP NOS Reference ELE/Q3108 QP NOS Name Field Engineer TV NSQF Level 4","selectable":true,"status":"active","industry_id":null,"canonical_role_id":null,"aliases":[{"text":"Field Engineer TV","lang":"en","source":"nco2015"}]}
{"source":"nco2015","code":"7421.1401","level":5,"parent_code":"7421","parent_source":"isco08","isco_major":"7","isco_unit":"7421","skill_level":null,"label_en":"Solar Panel Installation Technician","label_hi":null,"description_en":"Solar Panel Installation Technician is also known as `Panel Installer', the Solar Panel Installation Technician is responsible for installing solar panels at the customers' premises. The individual at work checks the installation site, understands the layout requirement as per design, assesses precautionary measures to be taken, installs the solar panel as per customer's requirement and ensures effective functioning of the system post installation.","selectable":true,"status":"active","industry_id":null,"canonical_role_id":null,"aliases":[{"text":"Solar Panel Installation Technician","lang":"en","source":"nco2015"}]}
{"source":"nco2015","code":"7421.1402","level":5,"parent_code":"7421","parent_source":"isco08","isco_major":"7","isco_unit":"7421","skill_level":null,"label_en":"Solar Photo Voltaic System Installation Technician","label_hi":null,"description_en":"Solar PV System Installation Engineer is responsible for designing and installing the solar photovoltaic system at the customer's premises to meeting their power requirement. The individual at work evaluates the installation site, designs the installation, plans and arranges for materials, and ensures smooth installation process. The individual also supervises the installation technicians' work. Qualification Pack Details: QP NOS Reference ELE/Q5902 QP NOS Name Solar PV System Installation Engineer NSQF Level 5","selectable":true,"status":"active","industry_id":null,"canonical_role_id":null,"aliases":[{"text":"Solar Photo Voltaic System Installation Technician","lang":"en","source":"nco2015"}]}
{"source":"nco2015","code":"7421.1403","level":5,"parent_code":"7421","parent_source":"isco08","isco_major":"7","isco_unit":"7421","skill_level":null,"label_en":"PV System Installation Engineer","label_hi":null,"description_en":"Solar PV System Maintenance Technician is responsible for maintenance and effective functioning of the installed solar panels. The individual at work cleans the installed solar modules, checks the photovoltaic system for uninterrupted power output and identifies faults in the PV system. Qualification Pack Details: QP NOS Reference ELE/Q6001 QP NOS Name PV System Installation Engineer NSQF Level 4","selectable":true,"status":"active","industry_id":null,"canonical_role_id":null,"aliases":[{"text":"PV System Installation Engineer","lang":"en","source":"nco2015"}]}
{"source":"nco2015","code":"7421.9900","level":5,"parent_code":"7421","parent_source":"isco08","isco_major":"7","isco_unit":"7421","skill_level":null,"label_en":"Electronic Mechanics and Services, Other","label_hi":null,"description_en":"Electronic Mechanics and Servicers, other include all other workers engaged in installing, servicing and repairing radios and television sets and other audio equipment, not elsewhere classified.","selectable":true,"status":"active","industry_id":null,"canonical_role_id":null,"aliases":[{"text":"Electronic Mechanics and Services, Other","lang":"en","source":"nco2015"}]}
{"source":"nco2015","code":"7422.0100","level":5,"parent_code":"7422","parent_source":"isco08","isco_major":"7","isco_unit":"7422","skill_level":null,"label_en":"Installation Mechanic","label_hi":null,"description_en":"Installation Mechanic (Telephone) installs telephone equipment in telephone exchange. Studies designs, blue prints, circuit diagrams and other specifications for installation of equipment to be done. Sets and installs switch board selector racks, relay set racks, automatic telephone system, key board, morse sets and tele printer as per plan and makes necessary electrical connections according to circuit diagram. Tests installation as prescribed to check mechanical and electrical adjustments of each component. Solders terminals of wires. Test checks operational efficiency and makes necessary adjustments. Installs batteries and battery charging equipment and fits and maintains protective devices. May install telephone sets at subscriber's premises.","selectable":true,"status":"active","industry_id":null,"canonical_role_id":null,"aliases":[{"text":"Installation Mechanic","lang":"en","source":"nco2015"}]}
{"source":"nco2015","code":"7422.0200","level":5,"parent_code":"7422","parent_source":"isco08","isco_major":"7","isco_unit":"7422","skill_level":null,"label_en":"Maintenance Mechanic","label_hi":null,"description_en":"Maintenance Mechanic (Telephone) tests, analyses defects, and maintains telephone equipment using test meters and hand tools. Tests wiring and operation of electrical and mechanical components of telephone apparatus, checks operational efficiency and locates faults using voltmeter, resistance meter, watt meter, capacity meter and other instruments as necessary. Replaces defective components, if required, and installs, repairs and adjusts equipment such as switches, relays amplifiers etc. using hand tools. Removes connections or wire distributing frames and solders wires to terminal lugs according to diagram. Conducts test checks periodically to maintain apparatus in operational efficiency. May maintain telephone- switching equipment at private establishments. May maintain and repair power apparatus and storage batteries.","selectable":true,"status":"active","industry_id":null,"canonical_role_id":null,"aliases":[{"text":"Maintenance Mechanic","lang":"en","source":"nco2015"}]}
{"source":"nco2015","code":"7422.0201","level":5,"parent_code":"7422","parent_source":"isco08","isco_major":"7","isco_unit":"7422","skill_level":null,"label_en":"Fault Management Engineer","label_hi":null,"description_en":"Fault Management Engineer is responsible for monitoring network from NOC location and maintaining network uptime by ensuring that faults are effectively resolved within shortest period of time. He is also responsible for directing and coordinating with the field team to carry out corrective/change activities on site in case field support is required. Qualification Pack Details: QP NOS Reference TEL/Q6500 QP NOS Name Fault Management Engineer NSQF Level 5","selectable":true,"status":"active","industry_id":null,"canonical_role_id":null,"aliases":[{"text":"Fault Management Engineer","lang":"en","source":"nco2015"}]}
{"source":"nco2015","code":"7422.0203","level":5,"parent_code":"7422","parent_source":"isco08","isco_major":"7","isco_unit":"7422","skill_level":null,"label_en":"Handset Repair Engineer (Level II)","label_hi":null,"description_en":"Fault Management Engineer is responsible for monitoring network from NOC location and maintaining network uptime by ensuring that faults are effectively resolved within shortest period of time. He is also responsible for directing and coordinating with the field team to carry out corrective/change activities on site in case field support is required.","selectable":true,"status":"active","industry_id":null,"canonical_role_id":null,"aliases":[{"text":"Handset Repair Engineer (Level II)","lang":"en","source":"nco2015"}]}
